<description>
Draw the red trace from its border marker, detouring around each blue/green bar it hits.

Input structure
- The grid has a background, one red marker on the border, and blue/green
  one-cell-thick bars perpendicular to the marker's inward direction.

Rule
- The red marker travels straight inward from its border.
- When the trace hits a blue bar, it passes around the bar on the left side
  relative to its direction of travel.
- When the trace hits a green bar, it passes around the bar on the right
  side relative to its direction of travel.
- Existing bars are preserved; only background cells on the trace become red.

Key insight
- The trace keeps the same overall forward direction; each hit bar only
  shifts the current lane by forcing a detour one cell before the obstacle.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single red marker pixel s on the grid border",
  "path": "straight inward ray from s; whenever the ray first hits a perpendicular blue/green bar, turn one cell before it and pass just outside the bar: blue chooses the left side relative to travel, green chooses the right side; then resume the same inward direction from the shifted lane until the boundary",
  "trajectory": "paint every background pixel on the ray and detour segments red",
  "transform": "keep the source marker and all blue/green bars unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-22 rows x 12-29 cols; rectangular, not square [observed]
  background: BLACK
  colors: BLACK, RED, BLUE, GREEN only
  src:
    single RED pixel on one border (top or left edge [observed])
    position: not at corner; interior position along the border edge
  bars:
    color: BLUE or GREEN; 1-cell-thick segments perpendicular to travel direction
    length: 2-3 cells (mostly 3) [observed]
    orientation: horizontal if travel is vertical, vertical if travel is horizontal
    count: 4-14 total; at least 1 of each color
    multiple bars may share the same perpendicular level (1-3 bars per level)
    bars on same level separated by gap >= 2 cells
    bars may touch grid border (dist=0 from edge)
  path:
    trace travels inward from RED marker toward opposite border
    hits 4-8 bars along the way; each hit detours around the bar
    BLUE bar: detour passes left side (relative to travel direction)
    GREEN bar: detour passes right side (relative to travel direction)
    detour: L-shaped -- stop 1 cell before bar, shift laterally past bar end, resume forward
    each detour shifts the lane; trace always reaches opposite border
    gap between consecutive hit levels along travel axis: 2-4 cells
    non-hit bars are scenery at same perpendicular levels but different lateral positions
  output: input + RED painted on all background cells along trace (including detour segments)

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (H x W) and travel direction (down or right).
    2. Place RED marker on the entry border at a random interior position.
    3. Simulate the full trace forward, placing bars constructively:
       a. Pick 4-8 hit levels with gaps of 2-4 along the travel axis; first level >= 2 from marker.
       b. For each hit level, pick BLUE or GREEN randomly. Compute the lateral shift direction.
       c. Place a bar (len 2-3) at that level so the trace's current lane intersects it,
          and the detour side cell is in-bounds and on background.
       d. Update the lane position after each detour.
    4. Optionally add 0-8 scenery bars at the same levels but at non-overlapping lateral positions
       (gap >= 2 from other bars on same level; must not intersect the trace path).
    5. Verify trace reaches opposite border in-bounds; reject if lane drifts out of grid.
    6. The input is the grid with RED marker + all bars (no trace). Output is produced by the solver.
```
